{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:51:24Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 167, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "36\t## Focus indicator design\n37\t\n38\t```css\n39\t*:focus-visible {\n40\t  outline: 2px solid #0066cc;\n41\t  outline-offset: 2px;\n42\t  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #fff;\n43\t}\n44\t```\n45\t\n46\t### Visual structure\n47\t\n48\t```\n49\t\u250c\u2500 2px white box-shadow ring\n50\t\u2502  \u250c\u2500 2px gap (outline-offset)\n51\t\u2502  \u2502  \u250c\u2500 2px blue outline\n52\t\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  \u250c\u2500 element boundary (border or edge)\n53\t\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  \u2502\n54\t[white][gap][blue][element]\n55\t```\n56\t\n57\tThe 2px white outer ring is imperceptible on light backgrounds but highly\n58\tvisible on dark ones. The 2px blue outline is visible everywhere. Together\n59\tthey create a focus indicator that adapts to its context.\n60\t\n61\t### Contrast computed (graphical elements, need 3:1 minimum)\n62\t\n63\t*Recomputed during design review \u2014 the previous draft's luminance figures had\n64\tarithmetic errors (most significantly `#16191c`, off by roughly 10x) that\n65\tmade several passing combinations look like failures. Figures below were", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_013U9eedLdMNjT4QCc6fR35h", "session_id": "79e2ac9d-8f8f-4122-ac4c-30abb4aa5ed1"}}
