{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:51:27Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 172, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "60\t\n61\t### Contrast computed (graphical elements, need 3:1 minimum)\n62\t\n63\t*Recomputed during design review \u2014 the previous draft's luminance figures had\n64\tarithmetic errors (most significantly `#16191c`, off by roughly 10x) that\n65\tmade several passing combinations look like failures. Figures below were\n66\tworked out by hand from the WCAG relative-luminance formula\n67\t(`L = 0.2126R + 0.7152G + 0.0722B` on linearized channels) and cross-checked\n68\tagainst known reference contrast ratios for similar colours.*\n69\t\n70\tLuminance values (relative, 0\u20131 scale, per WCAG formula):\n71\t- `#fff` (white): 1.0\n72\t- `#16191c` (near-black filter): 0.0095\n73\t- `#a8480a` (dark orange priority): 0.1299\n74\t- `#e8eaec` (light grey priority): 0.8179\n75\t- `#0066cc` (outline blue): 0.1386\n76\t\n77\t**Blue outline (`#0066cc`):**\n78\t- vs white `#fff` background: (1.0 + 0.05) / (0.1386 + 0.05) = **5.57:1** \u2014 comfortably passes\n79\t- vs near-black `#16191c`: (0.1386 + 0.05) / (0.0095 + 0.05) = **3.17:1** \u2014 passes on its own\n80\t- vs dark orange `#a8480a`: (0.1386 + 0.05) / (0.1299 + 0.05) = **1.05:1** \u2014 nearly invisible as outline alone (the two colours have almost identical luminance); white ring is the effective indicator here\n81\t- vs light grey `#e8eaec`: (0.8179 + 0.05) / (0.1386 + 0.05) = **4.60:1** \u2014 comfortably passes\n82\t\n83\t**White box-shadow ring (`#fff`), on dark backgrounds:**\n84\t- vs near-black `#16191c`: (1.0 + 0.05) / (0.0095 + 0.05) = **17.65:1** \u2014 excellent\n85\t- vs dark orange `#a8480a`: (1.0 + 0.05) / (0.1299 + 0.05) = **5.84:1** \u2014 comfortably passes (not a near-miss as previously calculated)\n86\t\n87\t**Combined effect:**\n88\t- **Light backgrounds (white, light grey):** blue outline alone already clears 3:1 (5.57:1 / 4.60:1); white ring is imperceptible here but not needed.\n89\t- **Near-black background:** blue outline alone clears 3:1 (3.17:1); white outer ring (17.65:1) is redundant but reinforces it.\n90\t- **Dark orange background:** blue outline alone is the one real near-miss (1.05:1, since the two colours are close in luminance), but the white outer ring clears 3:1 with margin (5.84:1) and is the effective indicator on this background.\n91\t- Every background/element combination meets or exceeds the 3:1 non-text minimum through at least one of the two rings \u2014 no colour value needs to change.\n92\t\n93\t## Behavioral changes (no visual design needed)\n94\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_018SKeV7qsMnrxLr45ru1dJQ", "session_id": "79e2ac9d-8f8f-4122-ac4c-30abb4aa5ed1"}}
