{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:52:04Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 195, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Edit", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01VEbZFsRmsixDg5H392vDm1", "input": {"replace_all": false, "file_path": "/home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/design.md", "old_string": "## Focus indicator design\n\n```css\n*:focus-visible {\n  outline: 2px solid #0066cc;\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #fff;\n}\n```\n\n### Visual structure\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500 2px white box-shadow ring\n\u2502  \u250c\u2500 2px gap (outline-offset)\n\u2502  \u2502  \u250c\u2500 2px blue outline\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  \u250c\u2500 element boundary (border or edge)\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  \u2502\n[white][gap][blue][element]\n```\n\nThe 2px white outer ring is imperceptible on light backgrounds but highly\nvisible on dark ones. The 2px blue outline is visible everywhere. Together\nthey create a focus indicator that adapts to its context.", "new_string": "## Focus indicator design\n\n```css\n*:focus-visible {\n  outline: 2px solid #0066cc;\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #fff;\n}\n\n.filter-option.active:focus-visible,\n.priority-select.priority-high:focus-visible {\n  outline: 2px solid #fff;\n  outline-offset: -4px;\n  box-shadow: none;\n}\n```\n\nThe second rule is a targeted override for the two dark-fill controls, and is\nnow part of the design rather than a developer improvisation \u2014 see\n\"Override for flush/dark-fill controls\" below.\n\n### Visual structure (global rule)\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500 2px white box-shadow ring\n\u2502  \u250c\u2500 2px gap (outline-offset)\n\u2502  \u2502  \u250c\u2500 2px blue outline\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  \u250c\u2500 element boundary (border or edge)\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  \u2502\n[white][gap][blue][element]\n```\n\nThe 2px white outer ring is imperceptible on light backgrounds but highly\nvisible on dark ones. The 2px blue outline is visible everywhere. Together\nthey create a focus indicator that adapts to its context.\n\n### Override for flush/dark-fill controls\n\nThe global rule's white ring is an outset `box-shadow`, which paints in the\n2px band *outside* the element's border box \u2014 over whatever sits behind it,\nnot over the element's own fill. That's fine when the band lands on a plain\npage/row background, but `.filter-option` buttons sit flush against each\nother with no gap and `overflow: hidden` on the parent (`App.css:58-64`), so\na focused button's outer ring can be clipped by that `overflow: hidden` or\nvisually occluded by the next button in DOM order painting on top.\n\nFor `.filter-option.active` and `.priority-select.priority-high`, use an\n**inset** white outline instead (`outline-offset: -4px`, no box-shadow). An\ninset outline is drawn inside the control's own border box, directly against\nits own fill, so it can't be clipped by a container or occluded by a flush\nneighbour \u2014 its visibility doesn't depend on what's behind the element at\nall. `.priority-select.priority-high` doesn't have the same flush-neighbour\nproblem as `.filter-option`, but gets the same treatment for consistency: one\noverride rule for both dark, spec-called-out backgrounds rather than two\ndifferent treatments for the same underlying \"outset ring may not read\nreliably\" concern.\n\n`.priority-select.priority-low` (light grey `#e8eaec`) and every other\ncontrol keep the global rule \u2014 the blue outline alone already clears 3:1\nthere (4.60:1, computed below), so no override is needed.\n\n**Contrast, inset white outline directly against the element's own fill:**\n- vs `.filter-option.active` (`#16191c`): (1.0 + 0.05) / (0.0095 + 0.05) = **17.65:1**\n- vs `.priority-select.priority-high` (`#a8480a`): (1.0 + 0.05) / (0.1299 + 0.05) = **5.84:1**\n\nBoth clear the 3:1 minimum with a wide margin, and \u2014 unlike the outset ring \u2014\nwithout any dependency on adjacent layout."}, "session_id": "79e2ac9d-8f8f-4122-ac4c-30abb4aa5ed1"}}
