{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:52:07Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 199, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "150\t   in place since only the Done button disappears. Developer handles.\n151\t\n152\t6\u20137. **AC6/AC7 \u2014 Edit cancel/save focus restoration:** after the edit form\n153\t   closes, focus returns to that row's Edit button. A `ref` on the Edit button\n154\t   + `useEffect` or imperative `focus()` call. Developer handles.\n155\t\n156\tSee `frontend/src/components/AddTask.jsx`, `TaskList.jsx`, `App.jsx` for\n157\timplementation points.\n158\t\n159\t## Component/prop wiring\n160\t\n161\t**AddTask.jsx** (`frontend/src/components/AddTask.jsx`):\n162\t- The task-title input already exists at line 26\u201331.\n163\t- Add `autoFocus` attribute to give it initial focus on page load (AC1).\n164\t- For the \"list empties\" fallback case (AC4), expose a ref or a method so `App.jsx` can focus it imperatively. Developer choice: either `useImperativeHandle` or a ref via `forwardRef` threaded to `App`.\n165\t\n166\t**TaskRow/TaskList.jsx** (`frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`):\n167\t- Each `TaskRow` component's Delete and Done buttons already exist (lines 134, 127).\n168\t- Add a ref to the Edit button (line 134) so focus can be restored after edit closes (AC6/AC7).\n169\t- After Delete button is clicked: compute next/previous focus target (in `App` or via callback) and call `.focus()` on that element (AC4).\n170\t- After Done button is clicked: same as Delete if the row disappears, or no-op if it stays visible (AC5).\n171\t- After edit form cancels or saves: call `.focus()` on the Edit button's ref (AC6/AC7).\n172\t\n173\t**App.jsx** (`frontend/src/components/App.jsx`):\n174\t- Maintain the task array (already does).\n175\t- For AC4/AC5 focus restoration, know which row index was deleted/completed, and compute the next focus target: `(index + 1 < tasks.length) ? tasks[index + 1] : (index > 0 ? tasks[index - 1] : null)`. If null, focus the AddTask input.\n176\t- Expose a method/ref so TaskRow can pass this logic via callback (e.g., `onFocusAfterDelete={(index) => { /* compute and focus */ }}`).\n177\t\n178\t## Styling (`frontend/src/App.css`)\n179\t\n180\tAdd one new rule at the end of the file:\n181\t\n182\t```css\n183\t*:focus-visible {\n184\t  outline: 2px solid #0066cc;\n185\t  outline-offset: 2px;\n186\t  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #fff;\n187\t}\n188\t```\n189\t\n190\t**Placement:** after all existing rules, so it applies globally to every interactive element (`<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`) without needing per-element selectors. The `*` is safe here because `:focus-visible` only applies to focused elements, so there is no blanket performance cost.\n191\t\n192\t**Width/offset choice:**\n193\t- `2px solid` outline is thick enough to be visible with the 2px offset even on similar-luminance backgrounds.\n194\t- `2px` offset creates breathing room on light backgrounds and improves visibility on dark backgrounds.", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01166FkZPMz2PpgeNRLxbezB", "session_id": "79e2ac9d-8f8f-4122-ac4c-30abb4aa5ed1"}}
{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:52:14Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 200, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Edit", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01DYcd9Lt3nDxQ9Nohz9WJtL", "input": {"replace_all": false, "file_path": "/home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/design.md", "old_string": "## Styling (`frontend/src/App.css`)\n\nAdd one new rule at the end of the file:\n\n```css\n*:focus-visible {\n  outline: 2px solid #0066cc;\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #fff;\n}\n```\n\n**Placement:** after all existing rules, so it applies globally to every interactive element (`<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`) without needing per-element selectors. The `*` is safe here because `:focus-visible` only applies to focused elements, so there is no blanket performance cost.", "new_string": "## Styling (`frontend/src/App.css`)\n\nAdd two rules at the end of the file:\n\n```css\n*:focus-visible {\n  outline: 2px solid #0066cc;\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #fff;\n}\n\n.filter-option.active:focus-visible,\n.priority-select.priority-high:focus-visible {\n  outline: 2px solid #fff;\n  outline-offset: -4px;\n  box-shadow: none;\n}\n```\n\n**Placement:** after all existing rules, so the global rule applies to every interactive element (`<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`) without needing per-element selectors, and the override rule that follows it wins on specificity for the two named selectors. The `*` is safe here because `:focus-visible` only applies to focused elements, so there is no blanket performance cost. See \"Override for flush/dark-fill controls\" above for why the second rule exists and its contrast numbers."}, "session_id": "79e2ac9d-8f8f-4122-ac4c-30abb4aa5ed1"}}
